.TH YT-UNSUB-DETECTOR 1 "November 2026" "YT Unsub Detector" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
yt-unsub-detector \- manage per-user Google Drive configuration
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B yt-unsub-detector
.RB [ config | status | \-\-version | \-\-help ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
The extension itself is installed and registered by APT. This command only
creates or inspects the current user's Google Drive configuration files.
Run it as the desktop user who owns the browser profile, not with sudo.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B config
Create private default configuration files if needed and print their paths.
.TP
.B status
Show the packaged version, configuration/key file paths, and whether a Drive link and
service account key are present. Private key contents are never printed.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/yt-unsub-detector/google-drive.json
Per-user Google Drive file link, stored as a JSON object with a link field or as a JSON string.
Defaults to $HOME/.config/yt-unsub-detector/google-drive.json.
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/yt-unsub-detector/service-account.json
Per-user Google service account key, read from beside google-drive.json.
.TP
.I /usr/share/yt-unsub-detector/extension
Read-only extension source used to build the registered CRX package.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Returns zero on success and nonzero on invalid input, unsafe paths, or filesystem errors.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR apt (8),
.BR dpkg (1)
.PP
/usr/share/doc/yt-unsub-detector/README.md.gz
